# ---- compiled TypeScript artifacts (2026-08-13) ----------------------------
# `tsc <file>` without --outDir emits JS NEXT TO the source. 424 such strays had
# accumulated across app/, crank/, indexer/ and writer/, and they were not
# harmless: vite resolves app/src/**/*.js ahead of the .tsx it was compiled
# from, and a stale app/vite.config.js shadows vite.config.ts entirely. The
# symptom is that `npm run build` succeeds once and then fails on every
# subsequent run with "Unexpected JSX expression" or a config-load error —
# a verification rule that silently stops verifying.
#
# The tsconfigs already set noEmit, so nothing SHOULD produce these; this is
# belt-and-braces so a stray bare `tsc` invocation cannot commit its output.
# Genuine hand-written .js (app/api/, app/scripts/) is unaffected — every path
# below is a directory that contains only TypeScript sources.
app/src/**/*.js
crank/**/*.js
!crank/deploy/**
indexer/src/**/*.js
writer/src/**/*.js
app/vite.config.js
# tests/ joined the list on 2026-08-15 after 70 strays reappeared there. Node
# resolves ./helpers to helpers.js before ts-node's .ts hook ever runs, so a
# stale compiled helper shadows the source the suite is supposed to be testing —
# edits land in the .ts and the run silently exercises the .js. The bankrun
# suite is the primary source of truth; a shadowed helper makes it lie.
tests/**/*.js

# Local endpoint log from crank/_local_sb_endpoint.ts (dev only).
crank/_sb_endpoint.log

# vC3 test runner transpile output (node --test consumes it; never committed)
mobile/test/out/

# Codex CLI config (carries a Colosseum PAT)
.codex/
